# ----- Composite figures -----
# A BARE `::: figure` opener is a composite figure (PART 9 S4c,
# markup-carve/carve#1215): the fence, its separator, the kind word, and
# NOTHING else. The same opener carrying a quoted title or a [label] is not
# that production and stays a generic container. The whole distinction is the
# tail of one line, so both readings are asserted here, and both directions -
# a positive alone would pass for a rule that claimed every `:::` line.

::: figure
# <- punctuation.definition.figure-group.carve
#   ^^^^^^ entity.name.type.figure-group.carve
#   ^^^^^^ markup.other.figure-group.carve
#   ^^^^^^ -entity.name.type.div.carve

![One](one.png)
^ Panel one.
# <- punctuation.definition.caption.carve
#  ^^^^^^^^^ markup.caption.carve

:::
^ The group caption, one line below the closing fence.
# <- punctuation.definition.caption.carve
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ markup.caption.carve

# A quoted title makes the line a generic container, not a group.

::: figure "Titled"
#   ^^^^^^ entity.name.type.div.carve
#   ^^^^^^ -entity.name.type.figure-group.carve
#          ^^^^^^^^ string.quoted.double.div-title.carve

# So does a [label], and so do both together.

::: figure [g]
#   ^^^^^^ entity.name.type.div.carve
#   ^^^^^^ -entity.name.type.figure-group.carve
#          ^^^ constant.other.reference.div-label.carve

::: figure "Titled" [g]
#   ^^^^^^ -entity.name.type.figure-group.carve
#          ^^^^^^^^ string.quoted.double.div-title.carve
#                   ^^^ constant.other.reference.div-label.carve

# THE SEPARATOR IS A SPACE RUN, NEVER A TAB (grammar.ebnf PART 7; corpus 254):
# `:::<TAB>note` renders as a paragraph, so the group scope must not claim the
# line below. It falls to the generic container rule, which over-colours it
# exactly as it always has.

:::	figure
# <- punctuation.definition.div.carve
# <- -punctuation.definition.figure-group.carve

# A longer fence opens a group just as three colons do.

:::: figure
#    ^^^^^^ entity.name.type.figure-group.carve

# `figures` is a different word, and a trailing word is not the kind word.

::: figures
#   ^^^^^^^ entity.name.type.div.carve
#   ^^^^^^^ -entity.name.type.figure-group.carve

